WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.819
before you ever display the output

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:03.340
of a predictive model in a

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.340
business review, you must explicitly

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.279
evaluate and display the historical

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:09.540
statistical uncertainty of that model.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.900
So you have to show its

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.840
track record. You have to show

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.720
the operator the model's past accuracy.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.200
Have these forecasts historically suffered

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.020
from model drift?

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.520
Is there bias in the legacy

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.240
data? you must give the human

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.060
operator the statistical basis for

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.580
deciding whether they should actually

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.320
trust this prediction enough to route

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.720
a hundred thousand dollar delivery

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.840
truck based on it.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.060
You never present a probabilistic forecast

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.860
as a deterministic fact.
